# Rust build output (Cargo.lock IS committed — this is an application/binary workspace)
/target
**/*.rs.bk
scenario-junit.xml

# Cargo.lock MUST be committed for reproducible builds and OSS supply-chain auditing.
# The explicit negation below ensures no parent .gitignore or future rule can accidentally
# suppress it (see GATE_0_CHECKLIST.md F-01 and final_audit_response_os.md).
!Cargo.lock

# IDE / editor directories
/.idea/
/.vscode/
/.ainxt/

# OS logs (generated at runtime — never commit)
/logs/
/eventlog/

# OS session history (generated at runtime — never commit)
/sessions/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
nul

# Temp Excel files
~$*.xlsx
~$*.xls

# Console-local state written by `ainxt-os`: the per-start jwt-sso signing secret, provider
# credentials, and the daemon log. Never commit it.
/.ainxt-console/

# Local runtime config generated by ./setup.sh from the shipped example. A deployment's own
# runtimed.toml holds its values — never commit one. The example it is copied from IS committed.
/runtimed.toml

# Environment / secrets
# .env.example IS committed (the template — safe to share).
# Any organisation-specific .env file holds deployment values — never commit one.
.env
.env.local
# deploy/.env
deploy/.env.*
!deploy/.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Test / runtime artifacts
/scenario-junit.xml

# NOTE: `docs/` is COMMITTED and published. The README states "Everything is in this
# repository; there is no external docs site" — that is only true if the 254-file docs site
# ships, so it must not be ignored here.
# NOTE: `.github` is COMMITTED. Ignoring it made it structurally impossible for this repo to
# carry CI, which is why a set of stale test assertions went undetected (see the release-readiness
# ledger, SETUP-004/SETUP-013).